# The one stable download URL. Cloudflare's static-assets runtime reads this file
# from the build output; Astro copies public/ into dist/ verbatim.
#
# It points at `latest/download` rather than a versioned asset so a release never
# needs a site deploy to become downloadable. That only works because CI uploads
# the asset as `Cupertino.zip` with no version in the name — see the release-app
# job in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# 302, not 301: the destination is expected to move (a different host, a mirror),
# and a cached permanent redirect would outlive the decision.
/download  https://github.com/mgcrea/mcp-cupertino/releases/latest/download/Cupertino.zip  302
/checksum  https://github.com/mgcrea/mcp-cupertino/releases/latest/download/Cupertino.zip.sha256  302
/releases  https://github.com/mgcrea/mcp-cupertino/releases  302
